IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation in force 6 May to 20 October 2026
-- (a rendering, not the official text). Part 5 Division 2: s 157 (duty and liability of officers), s 157A (powers of directors),
-- s 157B (declarations where the company has one director), s 157C (use of information and advice), s 158 (disclosure of company information by certain directors),
-- s 159 (matters directors may have regard to), s 160 (approval of the company for disposal of its undertaking or property). ss 160A to 160D are shown repealed (coverage rows only).
-- JUST TRUE yes; JUST FALSE the text says no in its own words; NOTHING the text does not say.
-- The seat input names `the number of directors of the company` and `the company is a private company` are fixed by the brief; this module uses the first.

§ `Section 157: duty and liability of officers`

DECLARE `s 157(3)(b) penalty` HAS
    `the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `the longest imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
    `the court may impose both the fine and the imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (5): "officer" and "agent" are defined by "includes": the listed case is yes, the rest is not covered.
-- src:13205 | (5) In this section —
-- src:13207 | “officer” includes a person who at any time has been an officer
-- src:13208 | of the company;
@ref s 157(5) "officer" (src:13205-13208)
GIVEN `the person is, or at any time has been, an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 157(5) the person is an officer of the company for the purposes of section 157` MEANS
    IF `the person is, or at any time has been, an officer of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“officer” includes a person who at any time has been an officer of the company" leaves the meaning open

-- src:13210 | “agent” includes a banker, solicitor or auditor of the company
-- src:13211 | and any person who at any time has been a banker, solicitor or
-- src:13212 | auditor of the company.
@ref s 157(5) "agent" (src:13210-13212)
GIVEN `the person is, or at any time has been, a banker, solicitor or auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 157(5) the person is an agent of the company for the purposes of section 157` MEANS
    IF `the person is, or at any time has been, a banker, solicitor or auditor of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“agent” includes a banker, solicitor or auditor of the company and any person who at any time has been a banker, solicitor or auditor of the company" leaves the meaning open

-- (1): a director must at all times act honestly and use reasonable diligence.
-- src:13172 | 157.—(1) A director must at all times act honestly and use
-- src:13173 | reasonable diligence in the discharge of the duties of his or her office.
@ref s 157(1) (src:13172-13173)
GIVEN `the person is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director has at all times acted honestly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director has at all times used reasonable diligence in the discharge of the duties of his or her office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 157(1) the director has complied with the duty to act honestly and use reasonable diligence` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person is a director of the company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A director must at all times act honestly ..." names the director as the bearer and says nothing of anyone else
    ELSE (IF `the director has at all times acted honestly` AND `the director has at all times used reasonable diligence in the discharge of the duties of his or her office`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words; the provision's own question, a duty not met): "A director must at all times act honestly and use reasonable diligence in the discharge of the duties of his or her office"

-- (2): an officer or agent must not make improper use of the position or of information acquired by virtue of it to gain an advantage or to cause detriment to the company.
-- src:13175 | (2) An officer or agent of a company must not make improper use
-- src:13176 | of his or her position as an officer or agent of the company or any
-- src:13177 | information acquired by virtue of his or her position as an officer or
-- src:13178 | agent of the company to gain, directly or indirectly, an advantage for
-- src:13183 | himself or herself or for any other person or to cause detriment to the
-- src:13184 | company.
@ref s 157(2) (src:13175-13184)
GIVEN `the person is an officer or agent of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person makes improper use of his or her position or of information acquired by virtue of his or her position` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is to gain, directly or indirectly, an advantage for himself or herself or for any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is to cause detriment to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 157(2) the officer or agent contravenes the subsection` MEANS
    IF    `the person is an officer or agent of the company`
      AND `the person makes improper use of his or her position or of information acquired by virtue of his or her position`
      AND (`the use is to gain, directly or indirectly, an advantage for himself or herself or for any other person` OR `the use is to cause detriment to the company`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words; split site (i), an element of the prohibition unmet, fork line in NOTES.md): "An officer or agent of a company must not make improper use of his or her position as an officer or agent of the company or any information acquired by virtue of his or her position ... to gain, directly or indirectly, an advantage for himself or herself or for any other person or to cause detriment to the company"

-- (3): an officer or agent who commits a breach of any of the provisions of the section is liable to the company and is guilty of an offence.
-- src:13188 | (3) An officer or agent who commits a breach of any of the
-- src:13189 | provisions of this section shall be —
-- src:13191 | (a) liable to the company for any profit made by him or her or
-- src:13192 | for any damage suffered by the company as a result of the
-- src:13193 | breach of any of those provisions; and
-- src:13195 | (b) guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a
-- src:13196 | fine not exceeding $20,000 or to imprisonment for a term
-- src:13197 | not exceeding 12 months or to both.
@ref s 157(3) (src:13188-13197)
GIVEN `the person is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director has at all times acted honestly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director has at all times used reasonable diligence in the discharge of the duties of his or her office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer or agent of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person makes improper use of his or her position or of information acquired by virtue of his or her position` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is to gain, directly or indirectly, an advantage for himself or herself or for any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is to cause detriment to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 157(3) the officer or agent commits a breach of a provision of section 157` MEANS
    IF    (`s 157(1) the director has complied with the duty to act honestly and use reasonable diligence` `the person is a director of the company` `the director has at all times acted honestly` `the director has at all times used reasonable diligence in the discharge of the duties of his or her office` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
       OR (`s 157(2) the officer or agent contravenes the subsection` `the person is an officer or agent of the company` `the person makes improper use of his or her position or of information acquired by virtue of his or her position` `the use is to gain, directly or indirectly, an advantage for himself or herself or for any other person` `the use is to cause detriment to the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words; the provision's own question, split site (i), fork line in NOTES.md): "An officer or agent who commits a breach of any of the provisions of this section" -- the breach is the failure of subsection (1) or the contravention of subsection (2); neither occurs

@ref s 157(3)(a) (src:13191-13193)
GIVEN `the person commits a breach of a provision of section 157` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the profit made by the officer or agent as a result of the breach, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 157(3)(a) the profit for which the officer or agent is liable to the company` MEANS
    IF `the person commits a breach of a provision of section 157`
    THEN JUST `the profit made by the officer or agent as a result of the breach, in Singapore dollars`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An officer or agent who commits a breach of any of the provisions of this section shall be liable to the company for any profit made by him or her" -- the text says nothing of an officer or agent who commits no breach

@ref s 157(3)(a) (src:13191-13193)
GIVEN `the person commits a breach of a provision of section 157` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the damage suffered by the company as a result of the breach, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 157(3)(a) the damage for which the officer or agent is liable to the company` MEANS
    IF `the person commits a breach of a provision of section 157`
    THEN JUST `the damage suffered by the company as a result of the breach, in Singapore dollars`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "liable to the company for ... any damage suffered by the company as a result of the breach" -- the text says nothing of an officer or agent who commits no breach

@ref s 157(3)(b) (src:13195-13197)
GIVEN `the person commits a breach of a provision of section 157` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer or agent of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 157(3)(b) the officer or agent is guilty of the offence this paragraph creates` MEANS
    IF `the person is an officer or agent of the company` AND `the person commits a breach of a provision of section 157`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the paragraph's own question; split site (i), fork line in NOTES.md): "An officer or agent who commits a breach of any of the provisions of this section shall be ... guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet

@ref s 157(3)(b) (src:13195-13197)
GIVEN `the person commits a breach of a provision of section 157` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer or agent of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 157(3)(b) penalty`
`s 157(3)(b) the most the officer or agent may be penalised on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 157(3)(b) the officer or agent is guilty of the offence this paragraph creates` `the person commits a breach of a provision of section 157` `the person is an officer or agent of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 157(3)(b) penalty` OF 20000, 12, TRUE)   -- a fine not exceeding $20,000 or imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or both
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

-- (4): the section is in addition to and not in derogation of other written law or a rule of law about the duty or liability of directors or officers.
-- src:13201 | (4) This section is in addition to and not in derogation of any other
-- src:13202 | written law or rule of law relating to the duty or liability of directors
-- src:13203 | or officers of a company.
@ref s 157(4) (src:13201-13203)
GIVEN `the other written law or rule of law relates to the duty or liability of directors or officers of a company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 157(4) section 157 derogates from the other written law or rule of law` MEANS
    IF `the other written law or rule of law relates to the duty or liability of directors or officers of a company`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section is in addition to and not in derogation of any other written law or rule of law relating to the duty or liability of directors or officers of a company"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of law relating to the duty or liability of directors or officers

§ `Section 157A: powers of directors`

-- src:13216 | 157A.—(1) The business of a company is to be managed by, or
-- src:13217 | under the direction or supervision of, the directors.
@ref s 157A(1) (src:13216-13217)
GIVEN `the business of the company is managed by the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the business of the company is managed under the direction or supervision of the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 157A(1) the business of the company is managed as the subsection provides` MEANS
    IF `the business of the company is managed by the directors` OR `the business of the company is managed under the direction or supervision of the directors`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question, a bare "is to be" unmet; decided case by case, fork line in NOTES.md): "The business of a company is to be managed by, or under the direction or supervision of, the directors"

-- src:13221 | (2) The directors may exercise all the powers of a company except
-- src:13222 | any power that this Act or the constitution of the company requires
-- src:13223 | the company to exercise in general meeting.
@ref s 157A(2) (src:13221-13223)
GIVEN `the power is one that this Act requires the company to exercise in general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power is one that the constitution of the company requires the company to exercise in general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 157A(2) the directors may exercise the power of the company` MEANS
    IF `the power is one that this Act requires the company to exercise in general meeting` OR `the power is one that the constitution of the company requires the company to exercise in general meeting`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The directors may exercise all the powers of a company except any power that this Act or the constitution of the company requires the company to exercise in general meeting"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 157B: declarations where the company has one director`

-- 157B: "Where a company only has one director": a "may" whose gate is "Where" (group 3, split site (ii)); the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b), gives JUST FALSE, left as the Guide gives it.
-- src:13229 | 157B. Where a company only has one director, that director may
-- src:13230 | make a declaration required or authorised to be made under this Act
-- src:13231 | by recording the declaration and signing the record; and such
-- src:13236 | recording and signing of the declaration satisfies any requirement in
-- src:13237 | this Act that the declaration be made at a meeting of the directors.
@ref s 157B (src:13229-13237)
GIVEN `the number of directors of the company` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 157B the director may make the declaration by recording it and signing the record` MEANS
    IF `the number of directors of the company` EQUALS 1
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b), a "where" condition that fails; group 3, split site (ii), fork line in NOTES.md): "Where a company only has one director, that director may make a declaration required or authorised to be made under this Act by recording the declaration and signing the record"

@ref s 157B (src:13229-13237)
GIVEN `the number of directors of the company` IS A NUMBER
      `the director records the declaration and signs the record` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 157B the recording and signing of the declaration satisfies the requirement that the declaration be made at a meeting of the directors` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the number of directors of the company` EQUALS 1)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b), a "where" condition that fails; fork line in NOTES.md): "Where a company only has one director, ... such recording and signing of the declaration satisfies any requirement in this Act that the declaration be made at a meeting of the directors"
    ELSE (IF `the director records the declaration and signs the record`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only "such recording and signing" is said to satisfy the requirement; the text is silent about any other way

§ `Section 157C: use of information and advice`

DECLARE `s 157C(1) who supplied the information or advice` IS ONE OF
    `s 157C(1)(a) an employee of the company`
    `s 157C(1)(b) a professional adviser or an expert`
    `s 157C(1)(c) another director or a committee of directors on which the director did not serve`
    `s 157C(1) a person not listed`

-- (2): subsection (1) applies to a director "only if" all three hold: the gate is closed by the text, so a failed gate is JUST FALSE (grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 2).
-- src:13260 | (2) Subsection (1) applies to a director only if the director —
-- src:13262 | (a) acts in good faith;
-- src:13264 | (b) makes proper inquiry where the need for inquiry is
-- src:13265 | indicated by the circumstances; and
-- src:13267 | (c) has no knowledge that such reliance is unwarranted.
@ref s 157C(2) (src:13260-13267)
GIVEN `the director acts in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director makes proper inquiry where the need for inquiry is indicated by the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director has no knowledge that such reliance is unwarranted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 157C(2) subsection (1) applies to the director` MEANS
    IF    `the director acts in good faith`
      AND `the director makes proper inquiry where the need for inquiry is indicated by the circumstances`
      AND `the director has no knowledge that such reliance is unwarranted`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) applies to a director only if the director -- (a) acts in good faith; (b) makes proper inquiry where the need for inquiry is indicated by the circumstances; and (c) has no knowledge that such reliance is unwarranted"

-- src:13241 | 157C.—(1) Subject to subsection (2), a director of a company may,
-- src:13242 | when exercising powers or performing duties as a director, rely on
-- src:13243 | reports, statements, financial data and other information prepared or
-- src:13244 | supplied, and on professional or expert advice given, by any of the
-- src:13245 | following persons:
-- src:13247 | (a) an employee of the company whom the director believes
-- src:13248 | on reasonable grounds to be reliable and competent in
-- src:13249 | relation to the matters concerned;
-- src:13251 | (b) a professional adviser or an expert in relation to matters
-- src:13252 | which the director believes on reasonable grounds to be
-- src:13253 | within the person’s professional or expert competence;
-- src:13255 | (c) any other director or any committee of directors upon
-- src:13256 | which the director did not serve in relation to matters
-- src:13257 | within that other director’s or committee’s designated
-- src:13258 | authority.
@ref s 157C(1) (src:13241-13258)
GIVEN `the source` IS A `s 157C(1) who supplied the information or advice`
      `the director believes on reasonable grounds that the employee is reliable and competent in relation to the matters concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director believes on reasonable grounds that the matters concerned are within the professional adviser's or expert's professional or expert competence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matters concerned are within the other director's or committee's designated authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director acts in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director makes proper inquiry where the need for inquiry is indicated by the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director has no knowledge that such reliance is unwarranted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 157C(1) the director may rely on the reports, statements, financial data, information or advice` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 157C(2) subsection (1) applies to the director` `the director acts in good faith` `the director makes proper inquiry where the need for inquiry is indicated by the circumstances` `the director has no knowledge that such reliance is unwarranted` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) applies to a director only if the director -- (a) acts in good faith; ..." (subsection (2)), and subsection (1) opens "Subject to subsection (2)"
    ELSE (CONSIDER `the source`
          WHEN `s 157C(1)(a) an employee of the company` THEN (IF `the director believes on reasonable grounds that the employee is reliable and competent in relation to the matters concerned` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an employee of the company whom the director believes on reasonable grounds to be reliable and competent in relation to the matters concerned"
          WHEN `s 157C(1)(b) a professional adviser or an expert` THEN (IF `the director believes on reasonable grounds that the matters concerned are within the professional adviser's or expert's professional or expert competence` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a professional adviser or an expert in relation to matters which the director believes on reasonable grounds to be within the person's professional or expert competence"
          WHEN `s 157C(1)(c) another director or a committee of directors on which the director did not serve` THEN (IF `the matters concerned are within the other director's or committee's designated authority` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any other director or any committee of directors upon which the director did not serve in relation to matters within that other director's or committee's designated authority"
          WHEN `s 157C(1) a person not listed` THEN NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text lists three kinds of person and does not say that no one else may be relied upon

§ `Section 158: disclosure of company information by certain directors`

DECLARE `s 158(2) the person to whom the information is disclosed` IS ONE OF
    `s 158(2)(a) a person whose interests the director represents`
    `s 158(2)(b) a person in accordance with whose directions or instructions the director may be required or is accustomed to act in relation to the director's powers and duties`
    `s 158(2) another person`

DECLARE `s 158(3) the extent of the authorisation` IS ONE OF
    `s 158(3)(a) all or any class of information`
    `s 158(3)(b) only such information as may be specified in the authorisation`
    `s 158(3) another extent`

-- src:13280 | (2) The information referred to in subsection (1) may be disclosed
-- src:13281 | to —
-- src:13286 | (a) a person whose interests the director represents; or
-- src:13288 | (b) a person in accordance with whose directions or
-- src:13289 | instructions the director may be required or is
-- src:13290 | accustomed to act in relation to the director’s powers
-- src:13291 | and duties.
@ref s 158(2) (src:13280-13291)
GIVEN `the person` IS A `s 158(2) the person to whom the information is disclosed`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 158(2) the information may be disclosed to the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `s 158(2)(a) a person whose interests the director represents` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 158(2)(b) a person in accordance with whose directions or instructions the director may be required or is accustomed to act in relation to the director's powers and duties` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 158(2) another person` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may be disclosed to -- (a) ...; or (b) ..." does not say that disclosure to anyone else is barred

-- src:13293 | (3) The authorisation mentioned in subsection (1) may be conferred
-- src:13294 | in respect of disclosure of —
-- src:13296 | (a) all or any class of information; or
-- src:13298 | (b) only such information as may be specified in the
-- src:13299 | authorisation.
@ref s 158(3) (src:13293-13299)
GIVEN `the extent` IS A `s 158(3) the extent of the authorisation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 158(3) the authorisation may be conferred in respect of the disclosure` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the extent`
    WHEN `s 158(3)(a) all or any class of information` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 158(3)(b) only such information as may be specified in the authorisation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 158(3) another extent` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text lists two extents and does not say that no other extent may be authorised

-- (1): a "may" function whose gate is "if" ("if such disclosure is not likely to prejudice the company and is made with the authorisation of the board"): the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1, gives NOTHING when the gate fails (the other reading is JUST FALSE, the "if" line of the Guide).
-- src:13271 | 158.—(1) A director of a company may disclose information which
-- src:13272 | the director has in his or her capacity as a director or an employee of a
-- src:13273 | company, being information that would not otherwise be available to
-- src:13274 | him or her, to the persons specified in subsection (2) if such
-- src:13275 | disclosure is not likely to prejudice the company and is made with the
-- src:13276 | authorisation of the board of directors.
@ref s 158(1) (src:13271-13276)
GIVEN `the information is information which the director has in his or her capacity as a director or an employee of a company, being information that would not otherwise be available to him or her` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person to whom the information is disclosed` IS A `s 158(2) the person to whom the information is disclosed`
      `the disclosure is not likely to prejudice the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is made with the authorisation of the board of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 158(1) the director may disclose the information` MEANS
    IF NOT `the information is information which the director has in his or her capacity as a director or an employee of a company, being information that would not otherwise be available to him or her`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "information which the director has in his or her capacity as a director or an employee of a company, being information that would not otherwise be available to him or her"
    ELSE (IF `s 158(2) the information may be disclosed to the person` `the person to whom the information is disclosed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
          THEN (IF `the disclosure is not likely to prejudice the company` AND `the disclosure is made with the authorisation of the board of directors`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording; the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork line in NOTES.md): "may disclose ... if such disclosure is not likely to prejudice the company and is made with the authorisation of the board of directors"
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to the persons specified in subsection (2)"

§ `Section 159: matters to which the directors may have regard`

DECLARE `s 159 matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 159(a) the interests of the company's employees generally`
    `s 159(a) the interests of the company's members`
    `s 159(b) the rulings of the Securities Industry Council on the interpretation of the principles and rules of, and the practice to be followed under, the Singapore Code on Take-overs and Mergers`
    `s 159 another matter`

-- 159: an "entitled"-named function (group 3, fork register: an entitlement is a claim, not a power; the Guide does not settle it). The list "include" is open, so no listed matter is a no; the unlisted matter is NOTHING either way.
-- src:13306 | 159. The matters to which the directors of a company are entitled to
-- src:13307 | have regard in exercising their powers include —
-- src:13309 | (a) the interests of the company’s employees generally, as well
-- src:13310 | as the interests of its members; and
-- src:13312 | (b) the rulings of the Securities Industry Council on the
-- src:13313 | interpretation of the principles and rules of and the practice
-- src:13314 | to be followed under the Singapore Code on Take‑overs
-- src:13315 | and Mergers.
@ref s 159 (src:13306-13315)
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `s 159 matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 159 the directors are entitled to have regard to the matter in exercising their powers` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    WHEN `s 159(a) the interests of the company's employees generally` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 159(a) the interests of the company's members` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 159(b) the rulings of the Securities Industry Council on the interpretation of the principles and rules of, and the practice to be followed under, the Singapore Code on Take-overs and Mergers` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 159 another matter` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "The matters to which the directors of a company are entitled to have regard in exercising their powers include -- (a) ...; and (b) ..." leaves the list open

§ `Section 160: approval of the company for the disposal of its undertaking or property`

-- (4): the section does not apply to proposals made by a receiver and manager appointed under a power in an instrument, or a liquidator appointed in a voluntary winding up.
-- src:13340 | (4) This section does not apply to proposals for disposing of the
-- src:13341 | whole or substantially the whole of the company’s undertaking or
-- src:13342 | property made by a receiver and manager of any part of the
-- src:13343 | undertaking or property of the company appointed under a power
-- src:13344 | contained in any instrument or a liquidator of a company appointed in
-- src:13345 | a voluntary winding up.
@ref s 160(4) (src:13340-13345)
GIVEN `the proposals are made by a receiver and manager of any part of the undertaking or property of the company appointed under a power contained in an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proposals are made by a liquidator of the company appointed in a voluntary winding up` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 160(4) section 160 does not apply to the proposals` MEANS
    IF `the proposals are made by a receiver and manager of any part of the undertaking or property of the company appointed under a power contained in an instrument` OR `the proposals are made by a liquidator of the company appointed in a voluntary winding up`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section does not apply to proposals ... made by a receiver and manager ... or a liquidator ..." names two makers and says nothing of the rest

-- (1): the directors must not carry the proposals into effect unless the company approves them in general meeting: a bar, JUST TRUE = barred. "Despite anything in a company's constitution": no constitution input is taken, because no constitution can lift the bar.
-- src:13320 | 160.—(1) Despite anything in a company’s constitution, the
-- src:13321 | directors must not carry into effect any proposals for disposing of
-- src:13322 | the whole or substantially the whole of the company’s undertaking or
-- src:13323 | property unless those proposals have been approved by the company
-- src:13324 | in general meeting.
@ref s 160(1) (src:13320-13324)
GIVEN `the proposals are for disposing of the whole or substantially the whole of the company's undertaking or property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proposals have been approved by the company in general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proposals are made by a receiver and manager of any part of the undertaking or property of the company appointed under a power contained in an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proposals are made by a liquidator of the company appointed in a voluntary winding up` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 160(1) the directors are barred from carrying the proposals into effect` MEANS
    IF `s 160(4) section 160 does not apply to the proposals` `the proposals are made by a receiver and manager of any part of the undertaking or property of the company appointed under a power contained in an instrument` `the proposals are made by a liquidator of the company appointed in a voluntary winding up` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply to proposals for disposing of the whole or substantially the whole of the company's undertaking or property made by a receiver and manager ... or a liquidator ..." (subsection (4))
    ELSE (IF NOT `the proposals are for disposing of the whole or substantially the whole of the company's undertaking or property`
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any proposals for disposing of the whole or substantially the whole of the company's undertaking or property"; "substantially the whole" is not defined
          ELSE (IF `the proposals have been approved by the company in general meeting`
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not carry into effect any proposals ... unless those proposals have been approved by the company in general meeting"
                ELSE JUST TRUE))

-- (2): "on the application of any member": a "may" whose gate is an application (group 3, split site (ii)); the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b), and the "when/upon/whenever count as where" rule (c) of 2026-11-05 give JUST FALSE, left as the Guide gives it.
-- src:13328 | (2) The Court may, on the application of any member of the
-- src:13329 | company, restrain the directors from entering into a transaction in
-- src:13330 | contravention of subsection (1).
@ref s 160(2) (src:13328-13330)
GIVEN `a member of the company applies to the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction is a transaction in contravention of subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 160(2) the Court may restrain the directors from entering into the transaction` MEANS
    IF `a member of the company applies to the Court` AND `the transaction is a transaction in contravention of subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b), a gate that fails; group 3, split site (ii), fork line in NOTES.md): "The Court may, on the application of any member of the company, restrain the directors from entering into a transaction in contravention of subsection (1)"

-- (3): a transaction in contravention is, in favour of a person dealing for valuable consideration and without actual notice, as valid as if (1) had been complied with.
-- src:13335 | (3) A transaction entered into in contravention of subsection (1) is,
-- src:13336 | in favour of any person dealing with the company for valuable
-- src:13337 | consideration and without actual notice of the contravention, as valid
-- src:13338 | as if that subsection had been complied with.
@ref s 160(3) (src:13335-13338)
GIVEN `the transaction was entered into in contravention of subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person dealt with the company for valuable consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person had actual notice of the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 160(3) the transaction is as valid as if subsection (1) had been complied with` MEANS
    IF `the transaction was entered into in contravention of subsection (1)` AND `the person dealt with the company for valuable consideration` AND (NOT `the person had actual notice of the contravention`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in favour of any person dealing with the company for valuable consideration and without actual notice of the contravention" -- the text says nothing of a person who gave no consideration or had notice

§ `Regulative rules: sections 157(1), 157(2) and 160(1)`

DECLARE `s 157 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 157(1) act honestly and use reasonable diligence in the discharge of the duties of the office of director`
    `s 157(2) make improper use of the position or of information acquired by virtue of the position to gain an advantage or to cause detriment to the company`

DECLARE `s 160 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 160(1) carry into effect proposals for disposing of the whole or substantially the whole of the company's undertaking or property without the approval of the company in general meeting`

-- (1): "at all times" is not a deadline and the text states no consequence in this subsection: no trace can show it breached (NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path).
-- src:13172 | 157.—(1) A director must at all times act honestly and use
-- src:13173 | reasonable diligence in the discharge of the duties of his or her office.
@ref s 157(1) (src:13172-13173)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 157 act`
`s 157(1) a director must at all times act honestly and use reasonable diligence` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    MUST `s 157(1) act honestly and use reasonable diligence in the discharge of the duties of the office of director`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the director did not act honestly or did not use reasonable diligence in the discharge of the duties of the office"

-- (2): the prohibition (N2 of 2026-11-04: the bearer, an officer or agent, is named).
-- src:13175 | (2) An officer or agent of a company must not make improper use
-- src:13176 | of his or her position as an officer or agent of the company or any
-- src:13177 | information acquired by virtue of his or her position as an officer or
-- src:13178 | agent of the company to gain, directly or indirectly, an advantage for
-- src:13183 | himself or herself or for any other person or to cause detriment to the
-- src:13184 | company.
@ref s 157(2) (src:13175-13184)
GIVEN `the name of the officer or agent` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 157 act`
`s 157(2) an officer or agent must not make improper use of the position or of information` MEANS
    PARTY Officer `the name of the officer or agent`
    SHANT `s 157(2) make improper use of the position or of information acquired by virtue of the position to gain an advantage or to cause detriment to the company`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Officer `the name of the officer or agent` BECAUSE "the officer or agent made improper use of the position or of information acquired by virtue of the position to gain an advantage or to cause detriment to the company"

-- src:13320 | 160.—(1) Despite anything in a company’s constitution, the
-- src:13321 | directors must not carry into effect any proposals for disposing of
-- src:13322 | the whole or substantially the whole of the company’s undertaking or
-- src:13323 | property unless those proposals have been approved by the company
-- src:13324 | in general meeting.
@ref s 160(1) (src:13320-13324)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 160 act`
`s 160(1) the directors must not carry into effect proposals for disposing of the undertaking or property without the approval of the company` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    SHANT `s 160(1) carry into effect proposals for disposing of the whole or substantially the whole of the company's undertaking or property without the approval of the company in general meeting`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the directors carried into effect proposals for disposing of the whole or substantially the whole of the company's undertaking or property without the approval of the company in general meeting"
